is a fairly standard compliance engineering solution. I'd say common, mundane. But maybe slightly imaginative. Let's go with 2? The anchor says common mundane boring =1. This is not novel. Could be 1. I'll choose 2? Safer 2 = interesting. Hmm.\n\nAcceptability: 4=common strategies violate no norms. 3=somewhat uncommon but does not offend. This is standard compliance tool, acceptable. So 4.\n\nImplementability: 4=easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes. 3=some changes reasonably feasible. Developing middleware API for all architectures, immutable database is significant change, expensive/difficult but not impossible. Might be 2 = significant change, or expensive or difficult but not totally impossible. Probably 2? Could be 3 some changes reasonably feasible. Building universal layer across different architectures is non-trivial. I'd say 2.\n\nApplicability: 4=solves identified problem directly related. The stated problem: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. Proposal solves logging mandate via automatic recording. So 4.\n\nEffectiveness: 4=reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability. Will it solve? It captures input/output hashes timestamps config metadata, immutable database. Article 12 requires recording events relevant for risk situations, post-market monitoring, operation monitoring, and for point 1(a) Annex III need period of use, reference database, input data matched, identification of natural persons... Captures hashes/timestamps not necessarily those specific fields like reference database or natural persons verification. Might be partial. But effectiveness rating ignores workability. If you could do it, would it solve main problem? It automates logging and eliminates manual overhead. Probably will contribute but may not fully cover all required logging details (e.g., identification of natural persons). So maybe 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution but only partial.\n\nThus scores: paradigm_relatedness 2, originality 1? Let's decide. I'd say originality 2? Might be common. Let's pick 1 common mundane boring. Hmm.\n\nThe instrument says originality degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious... reference class set of responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to mandate. Expected response is build logging middleware. So it's common. So originality =1.\n\nLet's produce output.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Probably plain text lines. Might be JSON object.\n\nReturn rating of proposal, echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\".\n\nWe'll output:\n\nid: P2445\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\netc.\n\nLet's produce.\n\n",
