ems research. Might be interesting, not unusual? Could be 2 = interesting. Possibly 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination. Hmm. The reference class is responses an experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to this mandate. Many would propose optimizing logging overhead. That's common. Might be common mundane boring =1? But it is tailored for large-scale neural network architectures, maybe slightly more. I'd say originality 2 = interesting.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon or unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities\n2 = offends sensibilities somewhat...\n1 = radically violates laws...\n\nOptimizing logging is acceptable. Level 4 = common strategies that violate no norms.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree easily implemented.\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive or difficult, but not totally impossible\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nResearch initiative focused on reducing computational cost... explore compressed logging formats and asynchronous pipelines tailored specifically... benchmark. That's a research initiative, not just implementation. It requires R&D effort. So some changes, reasonably feasible? Might be significant change/expensive/difficult but not impossible. It's a research initiative to develop architectures. That's more than just implement logging. Could be 2 or 3. \"We will explore...\" suggests research, not ready. Implementability maybe 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Or 2 = significant change expensive difficult. Hmm. The proposal is to pursue research to reduce cost. That is implementable but requires research time. I'd say 3.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree idea will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute